# Data Source: monad_pipeline

Looks up an existing pipeline in the organization by `id` or exact `name`, so a configuration can reference one that is managed elsewhere (another Terraform configuration, or the Monad UI) without hard-coding its UUID. To manage the pipeline, use the [`monad_pipeline` resource](../resources/pipeline.md).

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/data-sources/monad_pipeline/data-source.tf" }}

## Argument Reference

Exactly one of the following is required:

* `id` - (Optional) ID of the pipeline. Set exactly one of `id` or `name`.
* `name` - (Optional) Exact, case-sensitive name. Set exactly one of `id` or `name`. Names are unique per pipeline type in an organization.

No match is an error that lists some of the names that do exist; an ID that does not exist is an error.

## Attribute Reference

* `id` - ID of the pipeline.
* `name` - Name of the pipeline.
* `description` - Description.
* `enabled` - Whether the pipeline is enabled.
* `created_at` - When it was created (RFC 3339).
* `updated_at` - When it was last changed (RFC 3339).
* `managed_by` - `customer` for objects you create; `system` or `internal` for ones Monad maintains.
